feat: keep LSP warm when opening files from hunk, disable copilot
hunk spawns a fresh $EDITOR on every `e`, so LSP started from scratch
each time. The new hunk-editor wrapper (hunk's EDITOR) instead keeps a
headless nvim server per git repo and attaches a UI to it; `:q` from the
last window only detaches, `:qa` stops the server, and it exits on its
own after 30 idle minutes. Inside nvim, <leader>gdh runs hunk in a float
and `e` opens the file in that same nvim.

Copilot is no longer imported in nixvim; the module stays for re-enabling.
